# ── Upstream clones: reference checkouts, kept outside git ──
# AcidBox is MIT (c) 2022 copych — fetched via:
#   git clone --depth 1 --branch S3-regular https://github.com/copych/AcidBox.git
# Its firmware source IS vendored under firmware/AcidBox/, as MIT requires
# only that the copyright notice travel with it — see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
# The clone at the repo root is a pristine upstream copy, kept for diffing.
#
# Acid_Drip has NO upstream license, so it is NOT redistributed here. It is a
# gitignored reference clone, fetched via:
#   git clone https://github.com/lonesoulsurfer/Acid_Drip_Bassline_and_Drum_Synth.git
# See UPSTREAM.md.
/AcidBox/
/Acid_Drip_Bassline_and_Drum_Synth/

# AcidBox ships 2.5 MB of drum samples under data/. Those are samples rather
# than source, and their provenance is less clear than the MIT grant covers,
# so they are not committed. Copy them next to the sketch before building the
# LittleFS image. See firmware/README.md.
/firmware/AcidBox/data/

# ── Arduino build output ──
build/
*.elf
*.bin
*.map
*.hex

# ── LittleFS image (built from AcidBox data/, uploaded via esp32-littlefs-upload) ──
littlefs.bin

# ── Tooling scratch ──
.openchamber/

# ── Editor / OS ──
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Secrets ──
*.pem
*.key
!*.pub
__pycache__/
*.pyc
